      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Aprendizaje profundo</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Redes de memoria a largo plazo</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Redes neuronales</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Modelos de predicciÃ³n</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Flujo de trÃ¡fico</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Forecasting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Traffic flow</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Deep learning.</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Traffic forecasting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Neural networks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Prediction models</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:subject>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-REPAIR">[ES] Existen multitud de modelos que tratan de predecir la velocidad en vÃ­as urbanas e interurbanas, la contaminaciÃ³n acÃºstica provocada por el trÃ¡fico en ciudades o el flujo de trÃ¡fico urbano en base a datos histÃ³ricos de cÃ¡maras o del trÃ¡fico en los mÃ³viles de las personas. &#xA;&#xA;En este estudio, se trata de diseÃ±ar un modelo que sea capaz de predecir el flujo de trÃ¡fico en la ciudad de Valencia, EspaÃ±a, en base a los datos recogidos por unas espiras electromagnÃ©ticas repartidas por toda la ciudad. Con una buena predicciÃ³n se podrÃ¡ ser capaz de prever posibles atascos y ser capaz de evitarlos. El objetivo es diseÃ±ar un modelo basado en una red neuronal recurrente de tipo Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) para realizar la predicciÃ³n del flujo de trÃ¡fico en las diferentes calles de Valencia en las diferentes horas del dÃ­a asÃ­ como un estudio de la influencia de las caracterÃ­sticas utilizadas en la precisiÃ³n del modelo.</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-REPAIR">[EN] There are many models that try to predict the speed on urban and interurban roads, the noise pollution caused by traffic in cities, or even the flow of urban traffic based on historical data from cameras or traffic on people's mobile phones.&#xA;&#xA;The aim of this study is to design a model capable of predicting traffic flow in the city of Valencia, Spain, based on data collected by electromagnetic loops distributed throughout the city. With a good prediction it will be possible to foresee possible traffic jams, and also to avoid them.&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;A model based on a recurrent neural network of the Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) type has been designed to predict the traffic flow in the different streets of Valencia for the different hours of the day, as well as a study of the influence of the characteristics used in the accuracy of the model.</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
